{#-
  The docs home, as the 2026-10-01 design draws it: the title, then one
  card per thing a person comes to do, each linking the pages that do
  it; a pointer to the Quickstart for someone new; and the record's
  reference pages as a row of links. A card links only pages that
  exist (`docPages` leaves out a slug no page has yet), and a card with
  none is left out, so the home never links a page before it is written.
-#}
{%- set tasks = [
  { icon: "chart-line", title: "See how I am doing", product: "Ladder",
    text: "Your season as Elixir recorded it, one mode at a time: your battles, record and win rate week by week, and the deck you played most.",
    slugs: ["ladder"] },
  { icon: "users", title: "Run my clan", product: "Clan",
    text: "Your leaders write down how the clan runs. Elixir Clan reads the record against it and hands them the calls to make.",
    slugs: ["bring-your-clan", "standing", "clan-actions"] },
  { icon: "heart", title: "Follow my friends", product: "Friends",
    text: "Follow friends, watch any player, and get a Wednesday email on how each of them did.",
    slugs: ["follow-a-friend", "watch-a-player"] },
  { icon: "mail", title: "Get emails", product: "Emails",
    text: "What each email holds, when it lands, and the switch for every one.",
    slugs: ["email", "milestones", "turn-an-email-off"] },
  { icon: "bot", title: "Ask my AI", product: "MCP",
    text: "Connect Claude or any MCP client to your whole record. Which tool answers which question, and how to read the answers.",
    slugs: ["connections", "choosing-a-tool", "tools"] },
  { icon: "code", title: "Build on Elixir", product: "Developers",
    text: "Sign in with Elixir, the JSON API and integration keys, and running a collector of your own.",
    slugs: ["sign-in-with-elixir", "json-api", "integrations", "operators"] }
] %}
{%- set record = collections.docSections | docGroup("record") %}
<nav class="docs__crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><span aria-current="page">Docs</span></nav>
<h1 class="hero-title docs__title">Elixir docs</h1>
<p class="docs__lede">Elixir keeps your Clash Royale record and reads it back to you: in the console, in your clan, by email and through your own AI. Start with what you want to do.</p>

<div class="docs-tasks">
  {%- for t in tasks %}
  {%- set pages = collections.docs | docPages(t.slugs) %}
  {%- if pages.length %}
  <section class="docs-task" aria-labelledby="task-{{ loop.index }}">
    <div class="docs-task__head">
      <span class="docs-task__icon">{% icon t.icon, 17 %}</span>
      <h2 class="docs-task__title" id="task-{{ loop.index }}">{{ t.title }}</h2>
      <span class="docs-task__product">{{ t.product }}</span>
    </div>
    <p class="docs-task__text">{{ t.text }}</p>
    <div class="docs-task__links">
      {%- for d in pages %}
      <a href="{{ d | pageUrl }}">{{ d.data.navTitle or d.data.title }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="docs-new">
  {% icon "rocket", 18 %}
  <p><b>New here?</b> The Quickstart takes you from asking for access to your first answer: an account, your player, and your own AI agent connected.</p>
  <a class="btn btn--gold" href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart</a>
</div>

<section class="docs-ref" aria-labelledby="docs-ref">
  <div class="docs-ref__head">
    <h2 id="docs-ref">The record</h2>
    <span>what every number means, for people and agents alike</span>
  </div>
  <div class="docs-ref__links">
    {%- for d in record.pages %}
    <a href="{{ d | pageUrl }}">{{ d.data.navTitle or d.data.title }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-ref" aria-labelledby="docs-agents">
  <div class="docs-ref__head">
    <h2 id="docs-agents">For agents</h2>
    <span>these pages and the tool reference, read by a machine</span>
  </div>
  <dl class="outline">
    <dt><code>elixir_docs</code>, <code>elixir_examples</code>, <code>elixir_updates</code></dt>
    <dd>This documentation, the worked examples and What's new, read over the MCP connection itself: the index, one page, one section, or a word search. Start with <a href="/docs/choosing-a-tool">Choosing a tool</a> and the <a href="/docs/glossary">glossary</a>.</dd>
    <dt><code>elixir://docs/&lt;slug&gt;</code> and friends</dt>
    <dd>The same pages as MCP resources (<code>elixir://docs</code>, <code>elixir://docs/&lt;slug&gt;#&lt;section&gt;</code>, <code>elixir://examples</code>, <code>elixir://changelog</code>, <code>elixir://updates</code>, <code>elixir://cards</code>), listed lazily by clients that cache <code>tools/list</code>; the eleven examples are also prompts.</dd>
    <dt><a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> and <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a></dt>
    <dd>What this service is and where everything lives, in one short file; and every documentation page with the whole tool reference in one fetch.</dd>
    <dt><a href="/tools.json">/tools.json</a></dt>
    <dd>The tool registry as JSON: names, groups, descriptions, arguments, and the capability each one requires.</dd>
    <dt><a href="/api/public/stats">/api/public/stats</a></dt>
    <dd>Live corpus totals and the full-history daily series. No authentication.</dd>
    <dt><a href="/updates">Updates</a></dt>
    <dd>Every contract version and what shipped in it, the same list <code>elixir_changelog</code> returns.</dd>
  </dl>
</section>
